# warnings

## MODULE_LEVEL_DIRECTIVE

```text
[MODULE_LEVEL_DIRECTIVE] The semantics of the module level directive "use wtf" in "hoist-directive.js" may not be preserved when bundling.
   ╭─[ hoist-directive.js:1:1 ]
   │
 1 │ "use wtf"
   │ ────┬────  
   │     ╰────── module level directive may not be preserved
   │ 
   │ Help: For more information, see https://rolldown.rs/in-depth/directives#other-directives
───╯

```

# Assets

## hoist-directive.js

```js
"use wtf";

// hoist-directive.js
using a = b;

```

## hoist-export-class-direct.js

```js
// hoist-export-class-direct.js
using a = b;
var Foo1 = class {
	ac = [a, c];
};
var Bar1 = class Bar1 {
	ac = [
		a,
		c,
		Bar1
	];
};
using c = d;

export { Bar1, Foo1 };

```

## hoist-export-class-indirect.js

```js
// hoist-export-class-indirect.js
using a = b;
var Foo1 = class {
	ac = [a, c];
};
var Bar1 = class Bar1 {
	ac = [
		a,
		c,
		Bar1
	];
};
using c = d;

export { Bar1, Foo1 };

```

## hoist-export-clause.js

```js
// hoist-export-clause.js
using a = b;
using c = d;

export { a, c as "c!" };

```

## hoist-export-default-class-anonymous.js

```js
